      "status": "not-Lean-certified",
      "formula": "Ent_mu_n(h_n^2) <= (1/2) E_mu_n sum_i (h_n-h_n o flip_i)^2; h_n=f(S_n), S_n=sum_i(sign_i)/sqrt(n); actual entropy limit is Ent_gamma(f^2), actual flip-energy limit is4 E_gamma(deriv f)^2, giving coefficient2.",
      "mechanism": "Coordinate entropy controls assemble by true product entropy decomposition and RMS energy contraction; a law limit plus separately justified local perturbation-energy limit changes the ambient state space. This candidate records proof mechanism and adapter obligations; no Lean implication, equivalence or certified functor.",
      "hypothesis_map": "finite: Actual normalized counting law on all Fin n -> Bool, independent balanced coordinates; signed arbitrary h; all finite L1 domains produced.; limit: Actual normalized Rademacher sums, weak limit covariance1 gamma; for the compact core, real C2 compact-support f and genuine entropy/gradient limit producers, not supplied limits.; noncompact_source: Actual SPHMC sqrt density is C2 and noncompact; true cutoff mass/entropy/energy limits remain required. Gaussian law/orthonormal finite-product adapters are separate.",
      "conclusion_map": "finite: Entropy of h squared bounded by half of unnormalized sum of full coordinate-flip squares.; Gaussian: Entropy of f squared bounded by twice real derivative-square integral after the proven factor4 limit.; paper: Only after true finite-Hilbert/cutoff and canonical entropy/quarter-energy identity does this supply KL<=Fisher/2; no T2 or W2 from this bridge.",
      "failure_boundary": "No arbitrary dependent Boolean/Gibbs law, modified LSI jump entropy, covariance mismatch, noncompact extension without limits, canonical RN differentiation from AE equality, T2/W2/main/composition or unbounded cost transfer. CLT law convergence alone does not imply flip-energy convergence; the map is many-to-one and no theorem equivalence is asserted.",
      "source_ids": [
